# --- server ---
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
# Dev only: when 1 (and NODE_ENV != production), POST /api/:op trusts x-cb-* identity headers with NO
# verification (temporary until real auth at M2). The app refuses to boot with this on in production.
# DEV_AUTH=1
# MCP stdio bridge identity (bun run mcp): single static operator, local only. There is NO role
# variable — assertMembership() reads the authoritative role from the database.
# CB_MCP_PRINCIPAL=<uuid>
# CB_MCP_WORKSPACE=<uuid>

# --- database: Supabase (managed Postgres + pgvector) ---
# From Supabase -> Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string.
#
# APP connection = the dedicated NON-BYPASSRLS role `cb_app` (created by `bun run migrate`),
# via the TRANSACTION pooler. Username form: cb_app.<project-ref>. Port 6543.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://cb_app.<project-ref>:<cb_app-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# ADMIN connection = the `postgres` owner, via the SESSION pooler (port 5432 on the pooler host,
# username postgres.<project-ref>). Used ONLY by migrate.ts. The direct db.<ref>.supabase.co host
# is IPv6-only without the paid IPv4 add-on and fails to resolve on IPv4-only networks.
DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=postgres://postgres.<project-ref>:<db-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
# Password migrate.ts assigns to the cb_app role — must equal <cb_app-password> in DATABASE_URL.
CB_APP_DB_PASSWORD=<cb_app-password>
# SSL: 'require' encrypts but does NOT verify the cert; use 'verify-full' (with the Supabase CA) in
# production. The pooler is transaction-mode (prepared statements off).
DB_SSL=require
DB_TRANSACTION_POOLER=1
# Optional app-pool sizing (defaults shown):
# DB_POOL_MAX=10
# DB_IDLE_TIMEOUT=20
# DB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=30

# --- AI router (one door: src/ai/router.ts) ---
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# provider:model form. ZDR (zero data retention) is DESIGNED as a per-workspace toggle but is NOT
# IMPLEMENTED yet — every call passes zdr:false, so `data_collection: 'deny'` is never sent to the
# provider. The switch lands with the workspace settings UI in M5 (DECISIONS D12).
#
# Chat model is CHOSEN: DeepSeek via OpenRouter (DECISIONS D12.1). Anthropic (cost) and OpenAI's
# chat models are ruled out. There is no CODE default on purpose — silently defaulting would spend
# money on a provider you did not pick — so set it here:
CHAT_MODEL=openrouter:deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
# Reserved for M7 (compiled-truth synthesis). Read by nothing yet; set it now or when M7 lands.
FRONTIER_MODEL=openrouter:deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro
# Embeddings are a separate, already-locked call (D13) — OpenAI embeddings are fine here; only
# the chat model is restricted. Gates the vector(N) column + HNSW index — do not change without
# a re-embed migration.
EMBEDDING_MODEL=openai:text-embedding-3-small
EMBEDDING_DIM=1536

# --- auth (Google OIDC, M2) ---
# AUTH connection = the least-privilege `cb_auth` role (created by `bun run migrate`), via the
# TRANSACTION pooler. Used ONLY for login/onboarding writes — never on the /api/:op hot path.
# Username form: cb_auth.<project-ref>. Port 6543. Fatal on first use if unset.
DATABASE_AUTH_URL=postgres://cb_auth.<project-ref>:<cb_auth-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# Password migrate.ts assigns to the cb_auth role — must equal <cb_auth-password> above.
CB_AUTH_DB_PASSWORD=<cb_auth-password>
#
# APP_BASE_URL is the SINGLE source of truth for the OIDC redirect URI, the __Host- cookie decision,
# the CSRF origin check, and the dev-login loopback gate. It is printed at boot — register that exact
# string as the Authorized redirect URI in Google Cloud Console.
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Derived from APP_BASE_URL. Set this ONLY to override (two independent origin values drift into
# Google's redirect_uri_mismatch, the #1 OAuth setup failure).
# OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=
#
# Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application).
# See docs/auth-setup.md for the full runbook.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Signs the short-lived cb_oauth state cookie. MUST be >= 32 chars — generate with:
#   bun -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
# Fatal lazily on the first cookie sign/verify, so the offline unit suite still runs without it.
SESSION_SECRET=
#
# Absolute session lifetime. Refresh rotation is CUT from M2, so there is no reuse detection —
# a stolen cookie stays valid for this whole window. Sign-out-everywhere bumps principals.session_epoch.
SESSION_TTL_DAYS=7
INVITE_TTL_DAYS=7
#
# POST /auth/dev-login: mints a REAL session with NO Google verification. Five gates must all pass
# (DEV_AUTH=1, DEV_LOGIN=1, NODE_ENV explicitly dev/test, APP_BASE_URL explicitly loopback); the app
# REFUSES TO BOOT if DEV_LOGIN=1 and any of the others is false. Local development only.
# DEV_LOGIN=1
#
# Behind a proxy (Railway/Fly/Cloud Run) set this or req.ip is the proxy address and the /auth/*
# rate limiter collapses to ONE bucket for the whole fleet. 'loopback' or a numeric hop count.
# TRUST_PROXY=
# CI sets 1 so live-DB security tests FAIL instead of skipping.
# CB_REQUIRE_LIVE_TESTS=1
